      "content": "Task:\nAdd a request handler `handle_create_user(params)` in `app/api/handlers.py`.\n`params[\"name\"]` must be a string with 1 to 50 characters after trimming whitespace, and `params[\"email\"]`\na plausible email address. The handler creates the user with the next free integer id and returns\n`(201, user)` where user has `id`, `name` (trimmed) and `email`. It returns\n`(409, {\"error\": \"email already exists\"})` when a user with the same email, ignoring case, already exists, and\n`(400, {\"error\": \"invalid user\"})` for an invalid name or email. A created user must then be retrievable\nwith `handle_get_user`.\nAdd tests for the new handler to the project's test suite.\n\n\nWork step by step: inspect the relevant code, make the change, and check it. When you are finished, run\n`echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` as a command on its own."
